MATHEMATICAL FORMULATION & MANUAL CALCULATION METHODOLOGY

1. Annual Consumption Value Calculation (ABC Analysis)
To classify inventory items using the Pareto Principle, the annual consumption value (ACV) for each product is calculated by multiplying its annual order frequency by its unit price:
ACV_i = Q_i * P_i
Where:
- Q_i = Annual order quantity / picking frequency of product i
- P_i = Unit price of product i (in TL)

Products are sorted in descending order of ACV, and cumulative percentage is computed as:
Cumulative Percentage_n = ( Sum(ACV_1 to n) / Sum(ACV_1 to N) ) * 100

Classification thresholds applied:
- Class A: Cumulative percentage <= 80.0% (High value / High velocity)
- Class B: 80.0% < Cumulative percentage <= 95.0% (Medium value)
- Class C: Cumulative percentage > 95.0% (Low value / Low velocity)

2. Annual Travel Distance Calculation (Round-Trip)
In warehouse operations, picking distance is calculated as a round-trip (traveling from the dispatch area to the storage rack and back):
Distance_annual = Q_i * D_i * 2
Where:
- Q_i = Annual order quantity (number of picks)
- D_i = One-way distance from the dispatch/packing area to the assigned rack location (in meters)
- 2 = Round-trip multiplier (to and from pick location)

